---
// /what-we-treat/substance-use/benzodiazepines/: What-We-Treat-Content-Briefs.md §H. Sources in
// docs/content/what-we-treat-sources-substance.md. Rotation: Reviews only. Reviewed by Frank.
// Framed as the step after medically supervised detox (brief assumption).
import ServicePage from '../../../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../../components/NextSteps.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import { WWT, CATEGORIES, SUBSTANCE_PAGES } from '../../../data/treat.js';
import { conditionAbout } from '../../../lib/programSchema.js';

const path = '/what-we-treat/substance-use/benzodiazepines/';

const signs = [
  'You take more than prescribed, or sooner than scheduled',
  'Your prescription runs out early',
  'You get benzodiazepines from more than one source',
  'Anxiety or sleep gets worse when a dose wears off',
  'You can’t imagine facing the day without it',
  'You mix it with alcohol or other substances',
];

const how = [
  { icon: 'brain', title: 'Anxiety treated alongside', text: 'For many people, the anxiety came first. We treat it directly, with therapy and psychiatric care, instead of leaving it to return once the medication stops.' },
  { icon: 'pill', title: 'Psychiatric care built in', text: 'A Telemed Clinix provider evaluates you and manages psychiatric medication while you’re in treatment. Benzodiazepines aren’t used during the program.' },
  { icon: 'compass', title: 'Skills for hard moments', text: 'CBT and DBT skills help you handle anxiety, stress and sleepless nights without reaching for a pill.' },
  { icon: 'layers', title: 'The deeper work', text: 'Psychodynamic work and Internal Family Systems look at where the anxiety began, so skills rest on real understanding.' },
  { icon: 'users', title: 'One group, one facilitator', text: 'The same clinician leads your whole session, so trust builds and the conversation goes deeper.' },
  { icon: 'refresh', title: 'Practice in real life', text: 'You bring what happens at home and at work back to group, and we practice a different response together.' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'I have a prescription. Does that change anything?', a: 'A prescription is part of the picture, not the whole of it. During pre-screening we look at the dose, how often you take it and for how long, so we can recommend a level of care that’s safe for you.' },
  { q: 'Do I need detox before starting?', a: 'If you’ve taken benzodiazepines consistently for an extended time, usually yes. Stopping can carry real withdrawal risks, so medically supervised detox and stabilization come first. We’ll help you find it.' },
  { q: 'How will my anxiety be treated without benzodiazepines?', a: 'With therapy, skills and psychiatric care. Your Telemed Clinix provider manages psychiatric medication, and your therapists work on the anxiety itself. <a href="/what-we-treat/mental-health/anxiety/">Learn about anxiety and addiction treatment</a>.' },
  { q: 'Can I keep my other psychiatric medications?', a: 'Often, yes. Your provider reviews what you take and makes changes only when they’re clinically indicated, not just because you’re starting a program.' },
  { q: 'Does insurance cover benzodiazepine addiction treatment?', a: 'Most plans cover outpatient treatment, including Medicaid plans. We check your benefits for free before you start. <a href="/admissions/insurance/">See accepted insurance and payment options</a>.' },
];
---
<ServicePage
  path={path}
  metaTitle="Benzodiazepine Addiction Treatment in West Palm Beach"
  description="Outpatient treatment for benzodiazepine dependence in West Palm Beach after medically supervised detox. PHP, IOP and OP with psychiatric care included."
  crumbs={[WWT, { name: CATEGORIES.substance.name, href: CATEGORIES.substance.href }, { name: 'Benzodiazepine Addiction Treatment', href: path }]}
  h1="Benzodiazepine Addiction Treatment in West Palm Beach"
  subheading="When the medication for anxiety became its own problem."
  lead="Outpatient treatment for adults dependent on Xanax, Valium, Ativan, Klonopin and similar medications, usually after medically supervised detox. We treat the dependence and the anxiety underneath it, together."
  faqTitle="Frequently Asked Questions About Benzodiazepine Addiction Treatment"
  faqs={faqs}
  reviews
  about={conditionAbout('Benzodiazepine use disorder')}
>
  <!-- Signs -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid items-start gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Recognizing it</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Signs Benzodiazepine Use Has Become a Problem</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Prescribed doesn’t always mean safe for you</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">Many people start benzodiazepines for anxiety, panic or sleep, with a prescription. Dependence can build quietly. The fact that a medication was prescribed doesn’t, on its own, tell us whether it’s become a problem, or which level of care fits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card !p-7">
        <h3 class="text-xl">Some common signs</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          {signs.map((s) => <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check" class="mt-1 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-teal" />{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How we treat -->
  <section class="section bg-mist">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-5xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Treatment</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">How Sunview Treats Benzodiazepine Addiction</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">After detox, the work on what the pills were holding</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">Most people come to us once detox and stabilization are done. In PHP, IOP or OP, we treat the dependence and the anxiety underneath it at the same time. You also meet one-on-one with your primary therapist every week for 45 to 60 minutes, and free transportation to and from our center is available if you can’t drive yourself.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {how.map((h) => (
          <div class="card">
            <Icon name={h.icon} class="h-7 w-7 text-teal" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">{h.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2">{h.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Co-occurring + detox -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] border border-line p-7 sm:p-9">
        <Icon name="brain" class="h-8 w-8 text-teal" />
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl sm:text-[1.75rem]">Benzodiazepines and Co-Occurring Mental Health</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Anxiety is the most common concern alongside benzodiazepine dependence, and panic, trauma or depression often come with it. Treating the dependence without the anxiety leaves half the problem in place, so we treat both, with one team. We track anxiety with the GAD-7 throughout treatment, so you and your therapist can see what’s changing, and review your treatment plan together every month.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Read more about <a href="/what-we-treat/mental-health/anxiety/" class="font-bold text-teal underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">anxiety and addiction treatment</a> and <a href="/what-we-treat/dual-diagnosis/" class="font-bold text-teal underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">dual diagnosis treatment</a>.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] bg-cream p-7 sm:p-9">
        <Icon name="shield" class="h-8 w-8 text-teal" />
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl sm:text-[1.75rem]">When Detox Comes First</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">If you’ve taken benzodiazepines consistently for an extended time, stopping can carry real withdrawal and medical risks. Medically supervised detox, and often residential care, comes first so you’re stable before intensive therapy.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">We look at the dose, how often and how long during pre-screening, help you find detox if you need it, and plan Sunview as your next step.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextSteps
    title="Which Level of Care Fits"
    subtitle="Where most people start after detox"
    level={`<p>After detox, many people start in the <a href="/programs/php/">Partial Hospitalization Program</a> for daily structure while anxiety settles. From there they step down to the <a href="/programs/iop/">Intensive Outpatient Program</a>, day or evening, and then the <a href="/programs/outpatient/">Outpatient Program</a>. Our Clinical Director recommends where you start.</p>`}
    related={[
      { label: CATEGORIES.substance.label, href: CATEGORIES.substance.href },
      ...SUBSTANCE_PAGES.filter((p) => p.href !== path).map((p) => ({ label: p.label, href: p.href })),
      { label: 'Dual diagnosis treatment', href: CATEGORIES.dual.href },
      { label: 'All conditions we treat', href: WWT.href },
    ]}
  />
</ServicePage>
